===Etymology===
Neuter gender of supposed adjective ''*tribūnālis'', from {{m|la|tribūnus||tribune}}, from {{m|la|tribus||tribe}}. Equivalently, {{af|la|tribūnus|-al}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|tribūnal}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|tribūnal<3>}}

# a [[raise]]d [[semicircular]] or [[square]] [[platform]], on which the [[seat]]s of [[magistrate]]s were placed; {{l|en|tribunal}}, [[judgment seat]], [[dais]], camp platform
#* ''' 27 - 25 BC '''. [[w:Ab Urbe Condita Libri| Ab Urbe Condita]], [[w:Titus Livius|Titus Livius]], [https://archive.org/details/tliviihistoriar04livigoog/page/n106/mode/2up?view=theater|Book II, Chapter XII].
#*: {{ux|la|Ubi eo venit, in confertissima turba prope regium '''tribunal''' constitit.| When he came there, he was standing in the crammed crowd, near the king's '''tribunal'''.}}
# [[cenotaph]]
# {{lb|la|metonymy}} a [[court of law]], tribunal; [[judgment]]
# {{lb|la|by extension}} any platform used for [[purpose]]s other than above
# {{lb|la|by extension}} [[mound]], [[dam]], [[embankment]]
# {{lb|la|figuratively}} [[height]], [[greatness]]

